{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he spoke, etc. If it be with your soul, etc.</b> This may be explained along the path of the statement of Amram, of blessed memory (Bava Batra 36b), and this is their language: these of the house of the Exilarch do not establish a presumption of ownership, etc. And they gave the reason: because they are powerful (תקיפים), even though they have seized the land, the seizure of the field is of no avail to them, and it is removed from their hands." "<b>Now in the reply of the children of Heth they said</b> <b>a prince of Elohim</b>, etc., <b>from among us no man shall withhold his grave</b>, etc. — there are in their words two ways. The first is that he is exceedingly great and powerful, and does his will and desire, for none can stay his hand on account of his might; and accordingly he has no legal claim of seizure over the grave, and when they are able they will clear the dead from his grave. And this would signify that they do not want his dead to be buried before him unless he does it by force — and so the matter stands unresolved. \n\nThe second way is along this path: <b>a prince of Elohim</b>, etc. — meaning, you need not be concerned about the suspicion that applies to the house of the Exilarch, that their seizure is not a valid seizure, for the case is not comparable. The reason for the house of the Exilarch is that they are suspected of robbery and violence; but you are <b>a prince of Elohim</b> — meaning, your greatness is on account of the quality of your righteousness and the cleanliness of your hands, and there is no room for concern on this score, and your seizure is a valid seizure against which there is no claim. \n\nAnd perhaps it is to this that they intended in their saying <b>hear us</b> — meaning, understand our words, to where they lean. Therefore he said <b>if it be with your soul</b>, etc. — meaning, if your intention is in the straightforward sense of your words, that you wish to bury, etc. — <b>hear me and intercede for me with Ephron</b>, etc. But otherwise, the matter must be decided that the meaning of their words is according to the first interpretation, and they do not wish to bury, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:56.980076897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}